dsv41 patch 0090 (25.10.2026): pieces of the sudoingX recipe v2.0 engine, all OFF (in image v30, not used).
EXL3_L2PF_ORDER=1 (prefetch order + 8 MiB moe cap + 4 MiB LM-head prefetch; EXL3_L2PF_MOE_CAP_MB / EXL3_L2PF_HEAD_MB),
VLLM_SM12X_BMM_STREAMS=1 (recipe 0032), VLLM_DSPARK_MAIN_PROJ_ROWPAR=1 (recipe 0030, for our EXL3 K5 main_proj).
Measured on our workload (T=1 German prose, 2 x 2 interleaved fresh boots): 1 stream 56.0 vs 55.9 tok/s (noise), 4 streams
107.4 vs 110.2 (-2.5 %, all four runs below all four off runs; the extra prefetch competes with the routed experts' reads),
8 streams +0.8 %, sustained +0.6 %, T=0 7/8 identical. Left off.
